#### 7 · Sensitive Equality — `toStringFormat` (line 85)

```java
assertEquals("Catalog(items=1)", catalog.toString());
```

The assertion is coupled to the exact `toString()` format string. Any cosmetic change to `Catalog.toString()` (e.g., adding a field, changing delimiters) breaks this test even if behavior is correct.

**Refactor — assert on the semantic property instead:**

```java
@Test
void catalogReportsOneItemAfterAdd() {
    catalog.add("a", 1);
    // If toString coverage is truly needed, use contains:
    assertTrue(catalog.toString().contains("1"));
    // Better: add a size() method and assert on it directly.
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Brittle test that breaks on cosmetic refactors to `toString()`.

